note: Wordings from the "Still not English" list: the name of the student with the
note: highest score, have a score of at least 60, minus 10 percent, the most common name.
a student has a name, a class and a score.
let students be a list of a new student with name "Ana", class "Math", score 72,
    a new student with name "Ben", class "Math", score 95,
    a new student with name "Cleo", class "Art", score 51.
say the name of the student with the highest score, the class of the student with the lowest score.
say how many students have a score of at least 60, how many students have a score of 51.
if every student has a score of more than 50, say "Nobody below 51.".
let ben be item 2 of students.
if ben has a score of exactly 95, say "Ben has 95.".
let price be $80.
say price, minus 10 percent, 200, plus 5 percent.
let discount be 25.
say $8, minus discount percent, 10, minus 1 if discount is 25.
let drinks be a list of "latte", "tea", "mocha" and "mocha".
say the most common drink, the most common class in the classes of the students.
